#
#  Vtable for HRRR 3 km wrfprs (pressure-level file) as the boundary/initial-
#  condition source for the DrJack WRF chain (examples/cascades-hrrr-drjack.yaml,
#  HRRR_DRJACK_AB.md). One ungrib pass reads atmosphere, near-surface fields and
#  the 9-level RUC soil from the same wrfprs file; no second (soil) pass.
#
#  This is Vtable.RRFS with HRRR's sea-level pressure (MSLMA 0/3/198, as in
#  Vtable.raphrrr); every other row is the same NCEP GRIB2 coding in both files.
#
#  Deliberately NO SPECHUMD row. Vtable.RAP.pressure.ncep and Vtable.raphrrr both
#  read SPFH at 2 m; one 2 m SPECHUMD in met_em sets FLAG_SH, and real.exe then
#  builds QV from specific humidity on ALL levels -- the isobaric levels carry
#  only RH, so their SH is metgrid's fill value 0 and the whole column starts
#  bone dry (HRRR_DRJACK_AB.md section 6). With RH only, real.exe converts RH to
#  QV exactly as for NAM and RRFS.
#
#  Not extracted on purpose: p-level hydrometeors (the NAM chain never used them;
#  Vtable.HRRR.full has them for the nest).
#
